PI_CONTACT_INFO: Erin Delaria, NASA GSFC, Atmospheric Chemistry and Dynamics Lab, Greenbelt, MD 20771; erin.r.delaria@nasa.gov
PLATFORM: Dynamic Aviation King Air (N87Q)
LOCATION: East Coast, USA; Southern CA, USA.
ASSOCIATED_DATA: 10Hz PICARRO g2311f data also available. Aircraft position data in separate file.
INSTRUMENT_INFO: PICARRO 2401m 0.5 Hz CO2/CH4/H2O/CO and PICARRO 2311f 10Hz CO2/CH4/H2O. Sampling from common inlet (1/2" stainless steel with fluoropel coating) located under plane. Sample tube inner diameter 0.25", length about 25 feet, material FEP. Both instruments backed by a single IDP3 scroll pump.
DATA_INFO: Calibration: mixing ratios based on WMO-grade calibration NOAA cylinder IDs CC746186 and CA03516. GHG instruments are time-aligned through lag correlation, but data is not time-aligned to GPS. Time response of g2311f is 100 ms (1/e) based on lab pulse-decay experiments. Use slow data for absolute concentrations and fast data for fluxes. Do not use fast data for absolute concentrations. g2311f CO2 and CH4 data have been corrected for a pressure dependence using g2401m data
UNCERTAINTY: Accuracy (systematic uncertainty) is 0.2 ppm CO2, 0.004 ppm CH4, 1.3 ppb CO, and 2 ppm H2O. Precision (random uncertainty) is 0.03 ppm CO2, 0.0002 ppm CH4, 3 ppb CO, and 20 ppm H2O. When averaging, precision reduces as (number of points)^0.5, but accuracy does not reduce.
ULOD_FLAG: -7777
ULOD_VALUE: N/A
LLOD_FLAG: -8888
LLOD_VALUE: N/A
DM_CONTACT_INFO: Erin Delaria, NASA GSFC, erin.r.delaria@nasa.gov
PROJECT_INFO: NASA SARP and ALEGROS campaigns, Summer 2024
STIPULATIONS_ON_USE: Please contact the PI or DM for proper use. All NASA data use policies apply.
OTHER_COMMENTS: N/A
REVISION: R0
